{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Come on in, I'll get your vitals before Dr. Shah. Blood pressure is one eighteen over seventy four, and your pulse is ninety six.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay. Is that high? I don't know, I've been so jumpy.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (NURSE): It's okay for someone pregnant and nervous. I dipped your urine too, and the pregnancy test is positive.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah. That's why I'm here. There's spotting, and these cramps.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (DOCTOR): Hi, I'm Dr. Shah. I caught the tail end. Start wherever.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Um, so I'm pregnant, and I've been spotting, and my lower stomach cramps. I'm kind of freaking out.",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (DOCTOR): I hear you. When was your last period?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't know, doctor. The last period was around Diwali, or after. I never wrote it down.",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (DOCTOR): Okay, thinking out loud, Diwali was early November, so around then or a little after could put you near eight to ten weeks, but that is a guess, not a date we can trust.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): My cycles have been weird for ages. Sometimes I skip a month, sometimes it's, I don't know.",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (DOCTOR): Tell me about the spotting itself. When did you first see it?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): A couple of days ago. Like two days? I think. I don't know, doctor.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (DOCTOR): What color, and are you filling a pad?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): Pink. Sometimes a little red on the tissue. Not filling a pad. Just when I wipe, mostly.",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any clots, like clots you'd see with a period?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): No. No clots.",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (DOCTOR): And the cramps, where do you feel them, how strong?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Low down, like period cramps. They come and go. Maybe a four out of ten? Not, um, not doubling me over.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any fever, pain up in your shoulder, or a time you felt like you might pass out?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): No fever. No shoulder pain. I haven't fainted.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (DOCTOR): Nausea, throwing up, sore breasts?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): Nauseous in the mornings. I haven't thrown up. And, well, actually, my boobs are sore. I don't know if that's even related.",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (DOCTOR): It can be, this early. Any burning when you pee?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): No burning. I pee all the time, but I figured that's just being pregnant. I don't know.",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (DOCTOR): What are you taking at home?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): The pink prenatals, one of those a day. And these little white nausea pills. My OB called them Zofran. I let one dissolve under my tongue when I feel sick.",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (DOCTOR): Do you know the Zofran dose?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): Maybe four milligrams. I don't know, doctor. The bottle is on the counter at home.",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (DOCTOR): And the pink prenatals, are you actually getting one in every day?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): I forget some days. I skipped this morning. I don't know how many I miss in a week.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (DOCTOR): Ibuprofen, aspirin, anything like that?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): I was taking ibuprofen for my headaches, two hundred milligrams, but I stopped when the test was positive. Haven't touched it since.",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (DOCTOR): Good call. Any drug allergies?",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't know... maybe penicillin? I got itchy when I was a kid, I think. I'm not even sure it was the penicillin.",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (DOCTOR): I'll note a possible penicillin allergy, itching, not confirmed. Food allergies, latex?",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Nothing like that I know of.",
  "[SEG0037] person_3 (DOCTOR): Other medical problems? Surgeries?",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): I've had migraines for like five-ish years. No surgeries. Oh, my sister has a thyroid problem, hypothyroidism, and she takes biotin for her hair, but that's her, not me.",
  "[SEG0039] person_3 (DOCTOR): Got it, sister's thyroid issue, not yours. The biotin isn't yours either. Miscarriages or prior pregnancies?",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (PATIENT): One miscarriage, about two years back. Nothing since. I work at a dental office doing scheduling, I was supposed to be on the desk today, which is a whole other mess.",
  "[SEG0041] person_3 (DOCTOR): We'll keep this as short as we can. Do you smoke, or drink alcohol?",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't smoke. I had some wine before I knew I was pregnant, nothing since I saw the test.",
  "[SEG0043] person_2 (PATIENT): My boyfriend is out in the waiting room. Can he come in? I keep forgetting what you ask.",
  "[SEG0044] person_3 (DOCTOR): Yes. Let's get him.",
  "[SEG0045] person_1 (NURSE): I'll bring him back.",
  "[SEG0046] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Hey. Sorry, I was stuck with the parking app. She's been a wreck about this.",
  "[SEG0047] person_3 (DOCTOR): Thanks for coming in. How long have you seen the spotting?",
  "[SEG0048] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Since Sunday. That's four days. She always says it's less than it is.",
  "[SEG0049] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't know, maybe Sunday. I really thought it was a couple of days. I don't know, doctor.",
  "[SEG0050] person_3 (DOCTOR): So between about two days and four days, and we won't pretend we know the exact morning.",
  "[SEG0051] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Also, dumb question, I take a water tablet for my blood pressure, hydrochlorothiazide, twenty five milligrams. It was on the sink. She didn't take any, right?",
  "[SEG0052] person_2 (PATIENT): I didn't take your pill. I wouldn't. I don't know why that's in my head now.",
  "[SEG0053] person_3 (DOCTOR): His water tablet stays his. Not part of your list.",
  "[SEG0054] person_3 (DOCTOR): Let me put this together. Pink spotting, mild cramps, urine test already positive, vitals are steady. I was going to send you home and book an ultrasound for next week, maybe just repeat the urine today.",
  "[SEG0055] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): This morning though it looked brighter red, and she grabbed the left side of her belly. Scared me.",
  "[SEG0056] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah. The left side got sharper for a minute, then it backed off. I don't know if that matters. It's the same cramps, I think.",
  "[SEG0057] person_3 (DOCTOR): It matters. I'm changing the plan. Forget next week. I want a pelvic ultrasound today, and blood drawn today, a quantitative hCG, a blood count, and a type and screen.",
  "[SEG0058] person_3 (DOCTOR): On the belly first, since we're not waiting. Soft, with mild tenderness low down, a bit more on the left. No guarding, and I don't feel a mass. I'm skipping the speculum exam, the scan will tell us more than I will.",
  "[SEG0059] person_3 (DOCTOR): Working impression, not a diagnosis: this may be a threatened miscarriage. I also can't rule out an ectopic until that ultrasound. The dates are too fuzzy to call it eight or ten weeks for sure.",
  "[SEG0060] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay. I don't know what half of that means, but okay.",
  "[SEG0061] person_3 (DOCTOR): Threatened miscarriage means bleeding while the pregnancy might still be fine. Ectopic means outside the uterus, which we have to look for because of that one-sided pain. The scan and the bloods sort it out.",
  "[SEG0062] person_3 (DOCTOR): Don't restart the ibuprofen. If you need something for cramps, acetaminophen is all right. No sex until we see you with results.",
  "[SEG0063] person_3 (DOCTOR): If you soak a pad in an hour, the pain gets severe, your shoulder starts hurting, or you feel faint, come straight back, ER if the clinic is closed.",
  "[SEG0064] person_2 (PATIENT): Soak a pad, bad pain, shoulder, faint. I can remember that. I think.",
  "[SEG0065] person_3 (DOCTOR): I'll see you back here later today, after the scan, so we can talk about what it shows.",
  "[SEG0066] person_1 (NURSE): I can walk you to ultrasound and then the lab. They're both still open.",
  "[SEG0067] person_2 (PATIENT): Thank you. Um, my bag is under the chair, sorry, that's not medical. I'm ready."
 ],
